From d88d2dc0bbb5d664d0c0d77c1a74e0bd73b1a888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bohdan Chubuk <chbgdn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 01:26:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] netfilter: nft_flow_offload: Set hw_ifidx in
 nft_dev_fill_bridge_path()

When filling the bridge forwarding path, set the hw_ifidx field to
the hw_outdev ifindex. This is needed for the hardware offload path
in flow_offload_redirect() which uses hw_ifidx to find the redirect
device. Without this, hw_ifidx defaults to 0 and breaks PPE HW
offload on Airoha and MediaTek platforms.

Based on original backport fix for 6.18.y kernel where hw_ifidx has
not yet been consolidated into ifidx (unlike newer upstream).

Signed-off-by: Bohdan Chubuk <chbgdn@gmail.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
@@ -376,6 +376,7 @@
 	ether_addr_copy(th[dir].tuple.out.h_source, src_ha);
 	ether_addr_copy(th[dir].tuple.out.h_dest, dst_ha);
 	th[dir].tuple.out.ifidx = info.outdev->ifindex;
+	th[dir].tuple.out.hw_ifidx = info.hw_outdev->ifindex;
 	th[dir].tuple.xmit_type = FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT;
 
 	return 0;
